# Coding Guidelines & Best Practices

## Vue 3 Guidelines

### Component Structure
```vue
<script setup lang="ts">
// 1. Imports
import { ref, computed } from 'vue';
import type { Clip } from '../types/clip';

// 2. Props & Emits
interface Props {
  clip: Clip;
}

interface Emits {
  (e: 'updated', clip: Clip): void;
}

const props = defineProps<Props>();
const emit = defineEmits<Emits>();

// 3. Composables & Stores
const config = useConfiguration();

// 4. State
const loading = ref(false);

// 5. Computed
const displayName = computed(() => props.clip.displayName || props.clip.filename);

// 6. Functions
async function handleUpdate() {
  // ...
}

// 7. Lifecycle
onMounted(() => {
  // ...
});
</script>

<template>
  <!-- Template here -->
</template>

<style scoped>
/* Component-specific styles */
</style>
```

### Reactivity
- Use `ref()` for primitives
- Use `reactive()` for objects (but prefer `ref()`)
- Use `computed()` for derived state
- Use `toValue()` to unwrap `MaybeRefOrGetter<T>`

### Props
- Always use TypeScript interfaces
- Mark optional props with `?`
- Use `withDefaults` for default values
- Don't mutate props

### Emits
- Always define emit types
- Use descriptive event names
- Emit objects for complex data

## TypeScript Guidelines

### Type Safety
- Enable strict mode
- Avoid `any` type
- Use explicit return types on exported functions
- Define interfaces for all data structures

### Type Imports
```typescript
import type { Clip } from '../types/clip';  // Type-only import
import { updateClip } from '../services/clips';  // Value import
```

### Type Definitions
```typescript
// Use interfaces for objects
interface Clip {
  id: number;
  filename: string;
}

// Use type for unions
type ViewMode = 'grid' | 'grouped';

// Use enums for constants (or const objects)
const EDITOR_CONSTANTS = {
  DEFAULT_ZOOM: 1,
  MIN_ZOOM: 0.5,
} as const;
```

## API Service Pattern

### Service Functions
```typescript
// services/clips.ts
export async function updateClipName(id: number, displayName: string | null): Promise<Clip> {
  const { data } = await axios.patch<Clip>(`/api/clips/${id}`, { displayName });
  return data;
}
```

### Error Handling
- Let errors bubble to component level
- Handle errors in composables or components
- Show user-friendly messages via toast

## State Management

### When to Use Pinia Store
- Global state (auth, config)
- Shared data across routes
- Complex state with multiple actions

### When to Use Composables
- Reusable logic
- Component-specific state
- Side effects (keyboard shortcuts, drag and drop)

### When to Use Component State
- UI-only state
- Form inputs
- Local toggles

## Component Guidelines

### Component Naming
- PascalCase for components
- Prefix with context: `AppClipCard`, `BaseButton`
- Use full words, not abbreviations

### Component Size
- Keep components under 300 lines
- Extract complex logic to composables
- Create sub-components for complex UI

### Props vs Slots
- Use props for data
- Use slots for layout/content customization
- Name slots descriptively

## Styling Guidelines

### Tailwind Classes
- Use utility classes over custom CSS
- Group by category: layout, spacing, colors, typography
- Extract repeated patterns to components

### Custom CSS
- Use scoped styles
- Prefer CSS variables for theming
- Use CSS modules for non-Vue files

### Responsive Design
- Mobile-first approach
- Test all breakpoints
- Use responsive utilities: `md:`, `lg:`, etc.

## Performance

### Code Splitting
- Lazy load routes
- Lazy load heavy components
- Use async components for modals

### Virtual Scrolling
- Not currently implemented
- Consider for large lists (1000+ items)

### Image Optimization
- Use appropriate sizes
- Lazy load images
- Cache thumbnails

### API Optimization
- Debounce search inputs
- Cancel previous requests
- Use pagination

## Testing (Not Currently Implemented)

### Recommended Approach
- Unit tests for utilities and composables
- Component tests with Vue Test Utils
- E2E tests for critical flows
- API tests for backend

## Error Handling

### Client-Side
```typescript
try {
  await operation();
  toastStore.success('Success message');
} catch (error) {
  console.error('Operation failed:', error);
  toastStore.error('User-friendly error message');
}
```

### Server-Side
```typescript
// Use asyncHandler wrapper
clipsRouter.get('/:id', asyncHandler(async (req, res) => {
  // Errors automatically caught and handled
  const clip = await repo.findOneByOrFail({ id });
  res.json(clip);
}));
```

## Git Workflow (Recommendations)

### Commit Messages
- Use conventional commits format
- Examples:
  - `feat: add batch delete operation`
  - `fix: resolve video playback issue`
  - `refactor: extract clip actions to composable`
  - `docs: update API documentation`

### Branch Strategy
- `main` for production
- Feature branches: `feature/clip-collections`
- Bug fixes: `fix/video-seeking`

## Code Review Checklist

- [ ] TypeScript types are correct
- [ ] No console.logs in production code
- [ ] Error handling is present
- [ ] Loading states are shown
- [ ] User feedback (toasts) for actions
- [ ] Responsive design works
- [ ] No prop mutations
- [ ] Accessible (keyboard navigation, ARIA)
- [ ] Code is DRY (no duplication)
- [ ] Comments for complex logic

## Security

### Client-Side
- Never store sensitive data in localStorage
- Validate all user inputs
- Sanitize HTML (markdown library handles this)
- Use HTTPS in production

### Server-Side
- Verify Firebase tokens on all routes
- Validate all inputs
- Use parameterized queries (TypeORM handles this)
- Don't expose sensitive file paths

## Accessibility

### Keyboard Navigation
- All interactive elements tabbable
- Keyboard shortcuts documented
- Focus indicators visible
- Modal traps focus

### Screen Readers
- Use semantic HTML
- ARIA labels where needed
- Alt text for images
- Descriptive button text

### Visual
- Sufficient color contrast
- Don't rely on color alone
- Text resizable
- No flashing content

## Documentation

### Code Comments
- Explain WHY, not WHAT
- Document complex algorithms
- Add TODOs for improvements
- Keep comments updated

### JSDoc
```typescript
/**
 * Trims a video clip to the specified time range
 * @param clipId - ID of the clip to trim
 * @param startSec - Start time in seconds
 * @param endSec - End time in seconds
 * @returns Promise that resolves when trim is complete
 */
async function trimClip(clipId: number, startSec: number, endSec: number): Promise<void>
```

## File Organization

### Client
```
src/
├── views/           # Page components (one per route)
├── components/      # Reusable components
│   ├── App/        # App-specific
│   └── Base/       # Generic/reusable
├── composables/     # Reusable logic
├── stores/          # Pinia stores
├── services/        # API calls
├── types/           # TypeScript types
├── utils/           # Pure utilities
└── constants/       # Constants
```

### Server
```
src/
├── entity/          # TypeORM entities
├── actions/         # Business logic
├── routes/          # API routes
├── services/        # Core services
├── middlewares/     # Express middlewares
└── utils/           # Utilities
```

## Common Patterns

### Loading Pattern
```typescript
const loading = ref(false);

async function doSomething() {
  loading.value = true;
  try {
    await operation();
  } finally {
    loading.value = false;
  }
}
```

### Confirmation Pattern
```typescript
toastStore.confirm(
  'Are you sure?',
  async () => {
    await deleteClip();
  },
  'Confirm Action'
);
```

### Debounce Pattern
```typescript
const debouncedSearch = debounce((query: string) => {
  clipsStore.setSearch(query);
}, 300);
```

### Abort Pattern
```typescript
let abortController = new AbortController();

async function fetch() {
  abortController.abort();
  abortController = new AbortController();
  
  await axios.get('/api/clips', {
    signal: abortController.signal
  });
}
```

